    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41092" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίστροφ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>having dealings with,
				conversant,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἦν ἀνθρώπων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.177
				</span></i>
			 ; read by <i><span class="en">
				Ar.Byz.
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίσκοπος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				8.163
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινος</span>
			<i>concerned with</i> or <i>in</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				397
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστρεφής</span>
			, <i>curved, winding,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.979
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.P.
					75
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-φως</span>”
				<i>diligently, exactly,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ephipp.
					3.10
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Memn.
				7.3
			</span></i>.</div>
